` A checker for an instance, made of a kit its worker keeps (`checker-for`). `around` is the
` checker of the instance it is written in, which it types under; `probe` types it without
` checking it whole, as a probe or a checker that stands for a finished one does; `nested` types a
` body in place, in the function around it (`in-place`); and `trial` is the part of the body a
` trial types alone.
