+ do find-query-targets

` Numbers the targets of descendant queries once for the program, from 1, as the reference
` collects them before it compiles a class: the class `T` of each property a class with no
` type parameters declares as `Descendants'T`, then of each of its rules `whenever children T`
` and `whenever descendants T`, in the order of the modules and of what they declare, each
` once. Those a class with type parameters may add are noted (`note-open-targets`). Each target
` is completed, as the reference makes the class it collects, so the class's table holds its
` methods though no object of it is made.
if facts.query-targets-found
    =
facts.query-targets-found = true
for position in 0 .. < program.modules.length
    . owner = program.modules[position]
    . index = 0u32
    for decl in owner.decls
        do match? decl
            | .decl-class(class)
                if class.type-args.count == 0
                    . ref = DeclRef(position as ModuleId, index)
                    for member in owner.member-pool[class.members]
                        do match? owner.decls[member]
                            | .decl-property(property)
                                . query = if property.type-syntax != 0 then query-type(ref, property.type-syntax) else no-type
                                if query != no-type && !is-ancestor-query(query)
                                    . target = query-target(query)
                                    if facts.query-targets.find(target) == null
                                        facts.query-targets += target
                    for part in sheet-parts(ref)
                        . written = program.modules[part.module]
                        for member in written.member-pool[part-members(part)]
                            do match? written.decls[member]
                                | .decl-rule(rule)
                                    . target = trigger-target(part, rule.syntax)
