` class below takes its own value's type. A stored property's value is evaluated by the
` constructor of each class that holds it, and is typed for that class. A lazy property of a
` class is evaluated by one function, which the classes below share: its value is typed
` once, for the class that declares it, as the reference types it. So is a state machine a
` property of a class holds: the classes below that declare it no value of their own start
